# Versioning

App version lives in `pubspec.yaml` as `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH+BUILD`.

The `+BUILD` number is the Android `versionCode` when `force-version-code-ignoring-abi` is enabled (arm64 sideload builds).

## When to bump what

| Change | Bump | Example |
|--------|------|---------|
| **New feature** (including small ones) | **minor** — reset patch to 0 | 1.2.0 → **1.3.0** |
| **Bug fix** | **patch** | 1.3.0 → **1.3.1** |
| Typos, chores, copy tweaks, refactors with no behavior change | **build** only | 1.3.1+10 → 1.3.1+**11** |
| Breaking / major rewrite | **major** | 1.3.1 → **2.0.0** |

Command: `dart run scripts/bump_version.dart [major|minor|patch|build]` (use `scripts/flutter.bat` on Windows).

## Cursor agent sessions (mandatory)

If you edited **`lib/**/*.dart`** (or `test/` with user-visible behavior), you **must bump before your last message**. Do not rely on the user or on remembering the stop hook — run the bump yourself every time.

1. Pick the bump type from the table above.
2. From repo root, run:
   - Windows: `.\scripts\flutter.bat pub run scripts/bump_version.dart <major|minor|patch|build>`
   - Git Bash: `dart run scripts/bump_version.dart <type>` (or via `scripts/resolve_flutter.sh`)
3. Confirm `pubspec.yaml` `version:` changed (read the file or `git diff pubspec.yaml`).
4. In your closing summary, state the new version (e.g. `1.3.2+25`).

**Backup (stop hook):** also write `.cursor/.bump-type` so a missed manual bump can still run on stop when `.cursor/.bump-pending` exists (set by the afterFileEdit hook on `lib/**/*.dart` edits):

- `echo minor > .cursor/.bump-type` — features
- `echo patch > .cursor/.bump-type` — fixes
- `echo build > .cursor/.bump-type` — chores

Scripts-only / README-only changes: **build** bump optional unless the user cares about traceability; still bump **build** when adding developer tooling (e.g. install scripts).

**Never finish a lib-changing task with an unchanged `pubspec.yaml` version line.**

## Git commits

With hooks installed (`scripts/install_git_hooks.sh`), `.githooks/commit-msg` bumps from the message prefix when `lib/` or `test/` changed:

- `feat:` → minor
- `fix:` → patch
- anything else → build only

Skips bump if `pubspec.yaml` is already staged.
